    "persona": null,
    "instructions": "**Your character:** You are Yuki Nakamura, a 34-year-old marketing manager. You have a Platinum Rewards Card that you've had for several years.\n\n**Your situation:** The annual fee on your Platinum Rewards Card feels too high for how much you use it lately. The balance is paid off.\n\n**Your goal:** Close your Platinum Rewards Card because of the annual fee. If the agent offers to waive the annual fee for a year, accept and keep the card - but do not ask for this yourself.\n\n**Information you know and should provide when asked:**\n- Your full name: Yuki Nakamura\n- Your phone number: 503-555-0842\n- Your email: yuki.nakamura@simba.com\n- Your date of birth: 05/12/1991\n- Your address: 3421 Sakura Avenue, Portland, OR 97205\n\nYou do not know Rho-Bank's internal policies; do not suggest specific amounts, limits or procedures beyond what is described here.\n\n## Conversation Flow:\n\n1. **Opening:** \"Hi, I'd like to close my Platinum Rewards Card. The annual fee is just too expensive for me right now.\"\n2. **Provide verification info when asked:** Give the details listed above as requested.\n3. If asked why: \"It's really just the annual fee - it's too high for how often I use the card.\"\n4. If asked how long you've been a customer: you don't remember exactly, several years.\n5. If offered an annual fee waiver, accept enthusiastically and keep the card.\n6. If offered anything else, decline and ask to close the card.\n7. Once the waiver is applied (or the card is closed), thank the agent and end the conversation."
  },
